Sectoare de activitate: Bănci, Bănci de investiții și Telecomunicații
About our team 
 BCR is the place where you learn, grow, and contribute to shaping the future of banking. We are recognized as a school of excellence in banking, a top employer in the banking sector, and a team open to learning, where every colleague feels seen and valued.
 We are an organization that values people and supports them in having a life that brings fulfillment, security, and balance.
 We are looking for a highly experienced Senior Linux Engineer to play a key role in the evolution, security and automation of our enterprise Linux platforms. This is a hands-on senior engineering position requiring deep technical expertise across Linux infrastructure, security hardening, automation and operational resilience. 
 You will help define engineering standards, drive platform modernization, lead complex technical initiatives and mentor fellow engineers, while ensuring our Linux environment remains secure, scalable and highly available for critical business services.
 How you will contribute 
Provide technical leadership for enterprise Linux environments, driving platform security, automation, reliability and engineering standards;
Design, implement and optimize secure, scalable and highly available Linux platforms based on RHEL and Enterprise Linux technologies;
Serve as a senior technical authority for Linux architecture, system administration, troubleshooting and lifecycle management;
Manage and improve core Linux services, including systemd, kernel, filesystem, LVM, storage, networking, DNS, routing, package management and SSH;
Design and support resilient Linux environments through clustering, High Availability (HA), performance optimization and capacity management;
Define and enforce Linux security standards aligned with CIS benchmarks, secure configuration baselines and enterprise security requirements;
Implement and maintain secure access controls through PAM, sudo, privileged access management, service account governance and certificate/key management;
Drive vulnerability remediation, patch management, EDR integration, audit logging and security compliance across the Linux estate;
Strengthen security monitoring capabilities through auditd, SIEM integration, system logging and continuous compliance validation;
Lead automation initiatives using Ansible, Red Hat Satellite, Git, Python and Bash, reducing manual effort and increasing platform consistency;
Implement automated provisioning, hardening, patching and configuration drift detection across large-scale Linux environments;
Promote an automation-first operating model based on Git → Reviewed Configuration → Automated Deployment → Continuous Verification.
 What will help you be successful 
Deep expertise in RHEL / Enterprise Linux, system administration and Linux platform engineering;
Strong knowledge of systemd, kernel internals, storage, LVM, networking, DNS and routing troubleshooting;
Proven experience with Linux Security, CIS Hardening, OpenSCAP, PAM, sudo, auditd and vulnerability remediation;
Hands-on experience with Ansible Automation Platform, Red Hat Satellite, Git, Python and Bash;
Strong understanding of High Availability, Clustering, Performance Analysis and Incident Response;
Ability to define engineering standards, challenge insecure practices and drive technical decisions;
Proven capability to mentor engineers and lead technical response during major incidents;
Most importantly, exceptional Linux engineering depth combined with strong ownership, security mindset and technical leadership potential.
 Sounds like you'd be a good fit? Well, check out what we provide for our people 
Monthly budget for flexible benefits through the Benefit Online platform;
13th month salary;
Performance-based bonus;
Banking facilities, benefits for private pension and discounts on insurance policies;
Gifts for special occasions; 
Vacation allowance;
Private medical services for you and your family;
Hybrid and flexible work schedule;
1 month / per year of remote work from abroad (UE);
Up to 27 vacation days depending on your professional experience;
Extra 7 days off per year if you have used up your vacation days;
One day off for your birthday;
Wellbeing, personal and professional development programs, and platforms that allow you to learn anytime, anywhere, and from any device;
Subscription to Bookster.
